<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tem Binoka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tem Binoka was the ruler of the Kingdom of Abemama in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a> from the 1870s until his death in 1891. He ruled as an autocrat, controlling land, labour and the copra trade and dealing directly with European ships. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-louis-stevenson">Robert Louis Stevenson</a>, who stayed on Abemama in 1889, made him famous in his book In the South Seas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tem-binoka.jpg" alt="Tem Binoka" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Louis Stevenson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HM_King_Tembenoka_of_Apemama,_Kuria,_Arimaka.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
